    "lawCode": "Add §201-h, Lab L",
    "lawSection": "Labor Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S1961B\n\nSPONSOR: BROOKS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the labor law, in relation to requiring employers to\ndisplay a poster containing information on veterans' benefits and\nservices which shall be created and distributed by the department of\nlabor\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation is to direct the Department of Labor to\ncreate a standardized workplace posting that includes basic information\nabout veterans' benefits and services. Employers shall be required to\ndisplay this posting in an area accessible to employees.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. amends the labor law by adding a new section 201-h to direct\nthe Department of Labor to consult with the Division of Veterans'\nServices to create and distribute a veterans' benefits and services\nposter.\n\nSection 2. is the enacting clause.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe NYS Division of Veteran's Services is responsible for assisting\nVeterans in obtaining federal and state benefits that are already due to\nthem. These earned benefits have a massive impact on our veterans across\nthe state. Through its county offices, DVS brings in more than $2B for\nour veterans annually but, only reaches roughly 17% of eligible veter-\nans. By making public posting across the state, it is our hope to reach\nmore veterans who need access to their earned benefits or other impor-\ntant programs.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nMinimal\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect January 1, 2022. Effective immediately, the\naddition, amendment and/or repeal of any rule or regulation necessary\nfor the implementation of this act on its effective date are authorized\nto be made and completed on or before such effective date.\n",
